{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784202365,"nonce":"oCsoMq4OCg6CdRXHBj0v1CaiDkY=","title":"Mint a scoped forge token for the `clone` step and deliver it securely (ADR-0045 §Trust, §Token delivery). For a run, the control plane produces a **short-TTL (minutes), repo-scoped** token — **read-only for fork-PR runs** — and delivers it to the `scarab-clone` Pod via a tmpfs file under `/scarab/secrets/`, consumed by the image's `GIT_ASKPASS` helper. The remote URL persisted in `.git/config` stays credential-free (guarded by the S2 scrub check).","message":"Fork-PR runs reuse the same clone path but with the read-only token, bounded by the existing fork-PR secret lockout and restricted OIDC subject (`crates/scarab-server/src/lib.rs:2514-2526`).\n\n\n- [ ] A run mints a repo-scoped, short-TTL token; fork-PR runs get a read-only token\n- [ ] Token reaches the clone Pod only via tmpfs; never in env, URL, or argv\n- [ ] `.git/config` after clone contains no credential (S2 guard passes)\n- [ ] Fork-PR lockout path verified: fork run gets read-only token and cannot write\n- [ ] Token TTL is minutes, not the run lifetime\n\n\n- **GitHub App adapter** (installation-token exchange) — not yet designed (ADR pending; the 8 outbound `GithubForge` methods are `unimplemented!()`, `crates/scarab-forge-github/src/lib.rs:178-225`). Private-repo clone cannot ship before it; public-repo clone (S6) does not need this.","files":null}]}